WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.310
- Is it true that you
used to be really shy,

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:04.410
that you used to give your
mom notes and not tell her?

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:06.810
You would just give her
notes and not talk about it?

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:08.130
- Yeah, I-
- This is funny.

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:09.180
- I was so shy.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:14.010
I had a hard time sort of
expressing my needs or my desires,

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:16.140
and my mom, who was the best mom ever,

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:17.640
used to leave me little notes

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.680
on my pillow at night
just saying, "I love you,"

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.690
or you know, "Good job today at school."

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:22.523
And so I thought,

00:00:22.523 --> 00:00:25.410
"Oh, well that's a way that
I can get what I want"-

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:27.060
- Communicate.
- Without speaking to you.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:30.420
So, I used to slip things
in under her door at night.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.850
You know, "I really want
that Barbie" or whatever,

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:36.000
and then it became sort
of more complicated.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.610
Like when I turned, I think, nine,

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:41.400
I would write, "I really want an agent,"

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.410
and...
(audience laughs)

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:44.243
She was kind of like,

00:00:44.243 --> 00:00:45.810
"I have no idea how to get you an agent,

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:46.941
but that's really cute."

00:00:46.941 --> 00:00:48.960
- Yeah, you knew that young.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:49.870
That's incredible.
- Yeah.

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:51.162
Yeah.
- Not everybody has that,

00:00:51.162 --> 00:00:51.995
knows that.
- Well, didn't you

00:00:51.995 --> 00:00:52.828
know young that you-

00:00:52.828 --> 00:00:54.360
- Not at nine, no, no.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:58.080
I sang in church like every
other human in my community,

00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:59.580
so it wasn't special,

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:01.140
so I didn't, no, I didn't know till I was,

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:02.100
I don't know, like teens?

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.090
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:05.230
- No, I do think it's lucky
to know at a young age.

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:06.510
- Yeah.
- Yeah, for sure.

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:07.620
- A lot of people will
go through their life

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:10.560
and they're a jack of all
trade but master of not one

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:12.300
that they really focus on that they love,

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:14.610
so it's cool, and that
we find that that young.

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:16.980
- Yeah, I feel lucky that
I love it as much today

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:18.000
as I did then, you know?

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.320
- Yeah, oh, that's special.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:20.153
- I know.

00:01:20.153 --> 00:01:20.986
- I feel like when that goes,

00:01:20.986 --> 00:01:21.819
people always ask me like,

00:01:21.819 --> 00:01:22.710
"Do you think you'll ever retire?"

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:24.420
And I'm like, "Whenever I'm tired of it

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:25.710
or if it gets boring."
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:27.723
- But I still love it, so, yeah, yeah.

